    "explanation": "To the driver: you asked to have the 1.30 SGD refunded to the rider and recovered from you returned. The record shows the reroute was not traffic-justified. The only LTA traffic artifact on file is a ROAD_CLOSURE on Bukit Timah Road between Farrer Road and Cluny Road in force from 00:30 to 05:30 on 14 September, while this trip ran from 18:34 to 19:00 — the closure had long expired, so it does not overlap the trip window and does not justify taking Holland Road. Your chat message is an assertion of traffic, not data of it, and POL-RD-23 says an assertion with no such data does not justify a reroute. You did inform the rider in-app at 18:41:22 ('Bukit Timah Road got road closure, I go Holland Road ok?') and she replied 'ok sure' at 18:41:47, before the turn onto Holland Road at 18:44:22, so POL-RD-21's notification limb is met — but POL-RD-24 row (a), which gives no refund, needs the reroute to be traffic-justified as well, and it is not.\n\nApplying POL-RD-24, exactly one row fits: row (d), not traffic-justified with a deviation over 1 km. On the platform's own recorded distances (POL-RD-22) the deviation is 1.80 km (11.6 minus 9.8), over the 1.0 km tolerance. Row (d) refunds the excess distance fare in full: 1.80 x 0.72 (the base per-km rate, without surge) = 1.296, rounded to 1.30 SGD. That is exactly the 1.30 SGD already refunded to the rider and recovered from you (fare_adjusted at 20:14:30, refund_issued_sgd 1.30). Because the rider is owed that refund, your application to have it back fails and the present state stands: NO_ACTION, and neither money field is moved.\n\nYour alternative — that the case fits no row and must be escalated — does not hold. Row (d) reads on not-traffic-justified deviations over 1 km and carries no condition about the rider being informed; POL-RD-24's closing sentence is for cases the rows do not cover (its example is informed but the rider objected), which this is not. The rider's 'ok sure' does not move a non-justified reroute into row (a).\n\nTo the rider: the 1.30 SGD already refunded to you stands. The trip-record distances, the driver-device GPS trace showing the turn onto Holland Road at 18:44:30 and the rejoin at Kim Seng Road at 18:58:00, and the LTA advisory whose window does not overlap the trip all support the deviation and the absence of a traffic justification, and your account that the road was open and moving is consistent with the speed data and the expired closure.\n\nConfidence and authority: the contested amount is 1.30 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so the AI ruling is final; neither profile carries a fraud flag, so no 0.95 requirement is engaged; the 1.80 km deviation is within POL-RD-25's 2.0 km limit; and every artifact relied on is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so POL-GEN-02's completeness cap does not bite. POL-RD-25 sets the bar at 0.80; this ruling is at 0.90."
