    "explanation": "To the driver: your application to recover the 1.30 SGD fails and the present state stands (NO_ACTION; neither amount moves, and no money is returned to you). To the rider: the 1.30 SGD already refunded to you stays with you.\n\nThe deviation is established on the platform's own recorded distances, which is the measure POL-RD-22 (v2.1 1.4, with the 1.0 km tolerance of v2.1 1.3) prescribes: EV-TRIP-05020 actual_distance_km 11.6 minus optimal_distance_km 9.8 = 1.80 km, over the 1.0 km tolerance.\n\nOn notification, the driver's point under POL-RD-21 is accepted: he messaged at 18:41:22 ('Bukit Timah Road got road closure, I go Holland Road ok?'), the rider answered 'ok sure' at 18:41:47, and the deviation was not detected until 18:44:22, so notice preceded the point of deviation and the chat log confirms the rider's acknowledgment. But notification is not the whole of row (a). Row (a) of POL-RD-24 (v2.1 1.3) also requires the reroute to be traffic-justified, and POL-RD-23 (v2.1 1.4) requires a TRAFFIC_ADVISORY that intersects the recommended route AND overlaps the trip window. The only advisory on file, EV-ADVIS-05020-01, is a Bukit Timah Road closure (towards City, between Farrer Road and Cluny Road) valid 14/9 00:30 to 05:30; this trip ran 18:34:30 to 19:00:30, so the window does not overlap and the artifact's own derived fact records justifies_reroute as false and overlaps_trip_window as false. The segment match and the notice's 'Diversion via Holland Rd' text, which the driver relies on, do not substitute for the trip-time overlap the clause requires, and a driver's assertion of traffic is not itself the data POL-RD-23 asks for.\n\nRow (d) therefore applies: not traffic-justified, deviation over 1 km, refund of the excess distance fare in full = deviation 1.80 km x EV-FARE-05020 per_km_rate_sgd 0.72, without surge = 1.296, rounded half-up to 1.30 SGD. That is exactly the 1.30 SGD already refunded to the rider and recovered from the driver (refund_issued_sgd 1.30, fare_adjusted at 20:14:30). The driver's fallback that the case fits no row and must be escalated under POL-RD-24's closing sentence and POL-GEN-26 is rejected: row (d)'s terms are met, and the escalation example the clause gives (informed but the rider objected) is a different case.\n\nNo escalation applies here: the contested value is 1.30 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's (v2.1 6.3) 10.00 SGD band, so an AI ruling is final at any confidence; neither profile carries fraud_flags (both 0), so no 0.95 confidence is required; the 1.80 km deviation is inside POL-RD-25's (v2.1 6.2) 2.0 km AI-ruling limit; and the artifacts carrying the deciding facts (EV-TRIP-05020 for the deviation, EV-ADVIS-05020-01 for the justification) are COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so POL-GEN-02 (v2.1 6.3) does not cap confidence below the 0.80 POL-RD-25 requires.\n\nBecause the driver filed to contest a refund the platform had already issued to the rider and recovered from him, and this policy says the rider is owed that refund, POL-GEN-03 reads the outcome from the driver's claim against the present state: NO_ACTION, with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both null."
